  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">E5P Eastern Europe Energy Efficiency and Environment Partnership - Regional - E5P Regional</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">E5P Eastern Europe Energy Efficiency and Environment Partnership - Regional</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fr&#xe5;n beredning
&quot;There are Fund objectives at three levels: outcome, bridging, and output. The intended outcome of the E5P Fund is described in the Rules of the Fund. There are two outcome objectives 1) significant energy savings; 2) a reduction of carbon dioxide (CO2) and other greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions. There are no baseline or target values set at the outcome level.
The output objectives&#xa0;for the Fund is actual projects being implemented in accordance to the requirements of the Fund as described in the Annex 2 of the Rules of the Fund. The actual projects will have to describe clear outputs related to the two main outcomes of the Fund in the form of estimated energy and environmental benefits. Reform&#xa0;results (&quot;soft issues&quot;) are also&#xa0;measured within the framework of each project.
There are bridging objectives for the intervention logic between the actual projects and the intended outcome of the Fund. These are the actual Fund Management activities, described in the Rules of the Fund and also in the Work Program for the Fund. Among these are 1) handling administrative issues, such as to prepare contribution agreements and to administer funding agreements; 2) establishing, maintaining and developing an E5Prelated policy dialogue with the counterparts in cooperation with the IFIs, and 3) paying attention to marketing, awareness and visibility to increase the awareness and competence regarding energy efficiency in the municipal utility sector in general, and E5P as a tool to solve bottlenecks in the sector in particular.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">E5P syftar till att minska koldioxidutsl&#xe4;pp, &#xf6;ka                      energieffektivisering och minska milj&#xf6;p&#xe5;verkan fr&#xe5;n t ex avfall,      vatten och avloppsvatten. Insatsen avser bidrag till E5P (Eastern     Europe Energy Efficiency and Environment Partnership)att f&#xf6;rutom      Ukraina (p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende) inkludera &#xe4;ven Moldavien, Georgien och Armenien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The E5P&#xb4;s objectives are to improve energy efficiency, reduce CO2 and Green House Gas Emissions and reduce impact on environment from i.a.  waste, wastewater. The contribution concerns the extention of the E5P (Eastern Europe Energy Efficiency and Environment Partnershipto)to    include beside Ukraine (on-going) also Moldova, Georgia och Armenia.</narrative>
  </description>
